# Dev Notes 44 — Runtime Hardware Profile Registry v1

**Date:** 2026-06-17  
**Branch:** `runtime-hardware-profile-registry-v1`  
**Status:** Repo-verified on `runtime-hardware-profile-registry-v1` for the declared contract-only scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted hardware-profile contract smoke, existing contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael-run local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, and direct GitHub branch inspection passed. Direct GitHub `main` inspection remains a post-merge gate. No real-runtime test is required for the declared contract-only scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a contract-only hardware profile registry namespace under:

```text
runtime/profiles/
```

The namespace validates static hardware profile metadata for future routing, backend selection, model-bundle planning, capability admission, and hardware-aware compatibility work.

It makes the hardware-profile boundary explicit:

```text
requests and plans may select configured hardware profiles by hardwareProfileId
profile registry metadata describes hardware class, backend preferences, limits, media, and tuning hints
runtime/config hardware probing and init retry behavior remain separate runtime/lifecycle surfaces
```

This is not runtime execution. It does not probe hardware, load models, validate current machine capacity, call backends, call services, enqueue runtime requests, stream tokens, route `prompt()` through the Capability Bus, expose a public `executeAction()` API, or validate model-bundle/profile existence across registries.

