---

## 4. Modular design shape

The new namespace is intentionally split into small contract modules:

```text
hardwareProfileCommon.mjs        shared constants, copy helpers, field/key/path guard helpers, numeric guard helpers
hardwareProfileDefinition.mjs    single profile validation/normalization/assert helpers
hardwareProfileRegistry.mjs      registry validation, creation, listing, lookup, filtering helpers
hardwareProfileContract.mjs      thin re-export barrel
```

`runtime/profiles/` is a metadata contract namespace, not a runtime hardware probe namespace, not an init retry profile namespace, and not a backend execution namespace.

---

## 5. Contract behavior

The new contract exposes:

```js
validateHardwareProfileDefinition(profile)
normalizeHardwareProfileDefinition(profile)
assertHardwareProfileDefinition(profile)
copyHardwareProfileDefinition(profile)
validateHardwareProfileRegistry(registry)
normalizeHardwareProfileRegistry(registry)
assertHardwareProfileRegistry(registry)
createHardwareProfileRegistry(profiles)
listHardwareProfiles(registry)
getHardwareProfile(registry, profileId)
hasHardwareProfile(registry, profileId)
listHardwareProfilesForCapability(registry, capability)
listHardwareProfilesForBackendKind(registry, backendKind)
listHardwareProfilesForHardwareClass(registry, hardwareClass)
listSelectableHardwareProfiles(registry)
copyHardwareProfileRegistry(registry)
```

Profile definitions include:

```text
profileId
status
label
hardwareClass
capabilities
backendKinds
processModes
limits
tuning
media
metadata
```

Supported statuses:

```text
contract-only
planned
experimental
configured
disabled
deprecated
```

Selectable statuses:

```text
contract-only
planned
experimental
configured
```

Supported hardware classes:

```text
cpu-laptop
cpu-desktop
gpu-consumer
gpu-workstation
server-managed
external-service
unknown
```

Supported process modes:

```text
in-process-worker
managed-worker
oneshot-cli
service
external-service
metadata-only
```

`backendKinds` are validated as metadata strings in this registry contract version. Existing backend-adapter registry entries are not required. Model-bundle `defaultHardwareProfileId` existence validation remains future work.

